{"user": "so always try to control the edges", "user_ts": "2026-08-20T02:50:14.203423+00:00", "assistant": "Not **always**. Better rule:\n\n- **Corners** are best: once you get them, they can\u2019t flip.\n- **Edges** are good *if they\u2019re stable* or help you reach corners.\n- But edge squares next to empty corners can be dangerous \u2014 they may hand White the corner.\n- In the endgame, the biggest thing is often **mobility**: making White run out of good moves, even if you flip fewer discs now.\n\nSo: **control safe edges, protect corners, and don\u2019t chase flips.**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-20T02:50:16.911588+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-20T02:50:18.877371+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud"], "llama": ["Think Aloud"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["General Principle"], "consensus": ["General Principle"], "votes": {"General Principle": 3, "Local Justification": 1}, "confidence": {"General Principle": 1.0, "Local Justification": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["General Principle"], "sonnet": ["General Principle"], "llama": ["Local Justification", "General Principle"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false, "coarse": ["Direct Instruction"]}}
